+# `@deepseek-ai/dsh-electron-app`
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+The dsh desktop bundle. [`cordis.patch.yml`](cordis.patch.yml) layers over [`dsh-web-app`](../web-app/README.md), retaining its React client roster and Host APIs while replacing the physical browser carrier. It disables `web-startup`, `webserver`, `web-runtime`, client HMR, and the browser directory-picker chooser; changes Connection to `transport: electron`; and inserts the native Host and Client directory-picker halves.
+
+The bundle does not create an Electron window or IPC channel itself. [`@deepseek-ai/dsh-electron`](../../../apps/electron/README.md) owns that platform shell: it boots the resulting `desktop` profile, exposes the Host-composed Boot Graph and Connection operations through preload IPC, and serves built frontend and plugin assets through `dsh://app/`. This split keeps every business and UI plugin on the same composition graph as Web while the application shell alone owns Electron privileges.
+
+No row in this layer binds a port. The Connection Host service still provides its shared Fetch handler and stream sources, but the Electron main process calls them directly. The native directory chooser is appropriate because the operator and Host share one desktop.
+
+## Model Experience
+
+None, as the bundle changes only the human desktop carrier and browser UI composition.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+None; the composed model-facing rows remain owned by the base and Web bundles.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+- **Requires the Electron application shell** — booting this bundle in an ordinary browser leaves no Web server and no preload bridge.
+- **No client HMR** — the desktop protocol serves built plugin bundles and does not mount the Web rebuild stream.
+- **Native chooser assumes a local display** — remote or headless Host deployments should retain the browse directory-picker composition.
